diff --git a/changelog/69890.added.md b/changelog/69890.added.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f4df53e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/69890.added.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Added a ``low`` threshold to the :mod:`diskusage <salt.beacons.diskusage>` beacon so a mount
+can alert when usage unexpectedly drops, in addition to the existing high-usage alerting. This
+catches mounts that silently failed to mount, since the beacon would otherwise only see the
+empty directory on the root filesystem. Configure it alongside (or instead of) the existing
+threshold by mapping the mount to ``high``/``low`` keys instead of a bare percentage:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+    beacons:
+      diskusage:
+        - /mnt/nfs:
+            high: 50%
+            low: 5%
+
+Existing configuration that uses a bare percentage for a mount is unaffected and continues to
+behave exactly as before.
