@@ -83,6 +92,25 @@ def beacon(config):
     which means that if a regular expression matches another defined mount point,
     it will override the previously defined threshold.
 
+    A mount can also be configured with a mapping of ``high`` and/or ``low``
+    thresholds instead of a bare percentage. ``high`` behaves exactly like the
+    plain percentage form above, emitting a beacon when usage rises to or
+    above the threshold. ``low`` emits a beacon when usage falls to or below
+    the threshold, which is useful for detecting a mount that is normally
+    busy but has unexpectedly little usage, often a sign that the filesystem
+    failed to mount and the beacon is only seeing an empty directory on the
+    root filesystem.
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                high: 50%
+                low: 5%
+            - /mnt/always_busy:
+                low: 10%
+
     """
